<title>USA: Norwest unit sets $150 mln five-year notes.</title>
<headline>Norwest unit sets $150 mln five-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Norwest Financial was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER NORWEST FINANCIAL (NORWEST CORP AFFILIATE)</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	  COUPON 6.375 PCT   MATURITY 11/15/01</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	    ISS PRICE 99.983   FIRST PAY DATE 5/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY AA3	YIELD 6.378 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA-MINUS   SPREAD 27 BP	 CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>NOTE PRICED OVER FIVE-YEAR U.S TREASURY U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1672</p>
</text>
